$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_407F_2CCF';
<p>407f_2ccf</p> <h4>Three-Point Test Cross Problem</h4><p>A test cross is a way to explore the relationship between genes and their respective alleles. It is a useful tool for genetic mapping and deciphering the inheritance of traits. Specifically, a three-point test cross examines three (3) genes at the same time to learn about their assortment in gamete formation.</p><p>A standard three-point test cross involves crossing a heterozygous organism for all three genes with an organism that is homozygous recessive for all three genes</p> <p>For this problem, a test cross using a fruit fly (<i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>) heterozygous for three genes was conducted to understand their genetic interactions.</p><h6>Characteristics of Recessive Phenotypes</h6><p><ul><li><strong><span style="color: #9c3a1c;">Gene C</span></strong> is correlated with the '<span style="color: #9c3a1c;"><i>chummy</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #9c3a1c;">Gene C</span> shows behavior where it always maintains a close distance to other flies.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #1d6d53;">Gene D</span></strong> is analogous to the '<span style="color: #1d6d53;"><i>dewy</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #1d6d53;">Gene D</span> appears moist, with its body covered in tiny droplets of water.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #4852b4;">Gene K</span></strong> is affiliated with the '<span style="color: #4852b4;"><i>kidney</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #4852b4;">Gene K</span> has a body shape that is curved, similar to a kidney bean.</li> </ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid black;"><tr><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Phenotype</span></th><th colspan="3" align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Genotypes</span></th><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Progeny<br/>Count</span></th></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">chummy, dewy, kidney</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe4d9; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">c</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cbf5e7; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">d</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #eae7ff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">k</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">9</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">chummy, dewy</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe4d9; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">c</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cbf5e7; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">d</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #4852b4;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">75</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<sp